desc_stride	core library	Kani	discharged (Kani: slab::kani_desc_stride::desc_stride_reads_the_table)	contract 921200764, body 3955666860
# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): every access through a descriptor's
# permission (`DescPerm`) is made holding the lock whose value holds the
# permission (the class table's commit lock, then the taking arena's class
# lock), so successive holders are ordered by happens-before, the lock edge
# `lock::axiom_acquired` assumes, and per-location coherence
# ([intro.races]) gives each access the last write through the permission,
# `Relaxed` included; non-test slab.rs writes `state`, `shadow`, `arena`
# and `dirty_at` only in `init`, `set_state` and `set_dirty_at`
# (tests/loom/tests/access.rs). The slab model runs these bodies line for
# line, on a copy, and checks the class lock's edge to the next holder;
# its control shows a read outside the lock is stale.
SlabDesc::init	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: slab::loom_slab_desc_reads_through_the_lock; not checked: this body, which the model copies over loom's atomics, with one descriptor, two threads and the two locks; the lock edge, `lock::axiom_acquired`'s assumption; the hand-over between the two locks, which the model runs on one thread; that no write but these reaches the fields, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 204434904, body 42649987
